  "raw_text": "Step 1: Identify the base and height of the shaded triangle.\nThe base of the shaded triangle is 10 cm (the horizontal distance between the two parallel lines at the bottom).\nThe height of the shaded triangle is 3 cm (the vertical distance from the base to the peak of the triangle).\n\nStep 2: Use the formula for the area of a triangle.\nThe area \\(A\\) of a triangle is given by \\(A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}\\).\n\nStep 3: Substitute the values into the formula.\nSubstitute the base (10 cm) and height (3 cm) into the formula:\n\\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 3 \\]\n\nStep 4: Calculate the area.\n\\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 30 = 15 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{15}<|im_end|>",
